openai_raw_latex:
\begin{lemma}\label{clmmeasurables}
  Suppose that \(\aleph_0<\kappa<\lambda\) and both \(\kappa\) and \(\lambda\) are measurable.
  Then \({\rm Gal}(\mathscr{U},\lambda,\lambda)\) holds whenever \(\mathscr{U}\) is a normal ultrafilter over \(\kappa\).
\end{lemma}

\begin{lemma} \label{clmsamecof}
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item [$(a)$] If \(\kappa={\rm cf(\lambda)}\) then \(\binom{\lambda}{\kappa}\nrightarrow\binom{\lambda}{\kappa}\).
    \item [$(b)$] If \({\rm Gal}(\mathscr{D}_\kappa,\lambda,\lambda)\) holds then \(\binom{\lambda}{\kappa}\rightarrow\binom{\lambda}{\kappa}\).
    \item [$(c)$] If \(\kappa={\rm cf(\lambda)}\) then \(\neg{\rm Gal}(\mathscr{D}_\kappa,\lambda,\lambda)\).
  \end{enumerate}
\end{lemma}

Gold_Standard_raw_latex:
\begin{lemma} \label{L: possible weights}
Let $\EKR$ be a maximal coclique of $\Gamma_{2n}$.
    Let $B$ be an $n$-space of $\PG(2n,q)$ that occurs in a flag of $\EKR$. There exists a $k\in\{1,\ldots,n+1\}$, such that the number of flags in $\EKR$ that contain $B$ is precisely $\Gauss{k}{1}$. Furthermore, the number in question is $\Gauss{n+1}{1}$ if and only if every flag $(A',B')\in \EKR$ satisfies $A'\cap B\neq \emptyset$.
\end{lemma}

